  "configuration_id": "config_018",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only with multiprofile + avgpool (config_002, acc=0.591) is the clear best so far, while image-only ResNet50 is very weak (config_010, acc=0.208). Aggregation method matters (avgpool > transformer by ~7 pts) and multiprofile > singleprofile by ~10 pts. Key uncertainty: whether adding the image modality to the best RNA configuration provides any complementary signal, or whether the weak image features merely add noise. This experiment (config_018) directly extends the best unimodal config by adding ResNet50 image features via simple concat fusion, keeping all other settings at their best-known values (multiprofile, PCA n2000, avgpool). It is the most informative next step because it answers the central question of the multimodal study—does fusion help at all—using the simplest fusion mechanism as a baseline. If concat fusion improves over 0.591, we gain a strong direction to explore weighted fusion and stronger image encoders; if it does not, we learn to focus budget on RNA encoder improvements (scvi, scGPT) rather than multimodal combinations."
}

